+## Original ordinary failure and limited repair
+
+The first attempt completed four children with returncode0 and empty stderr:
+core lint, wrapper lint, p0 compile and p0 simulation. The TB printed its p0
+PASS for 160 main frames and 15 complete recoveries, then Icarus appended
+`sim/tb_ram_byte_write_coalescer.sv:317: $finish called at 29457000 (1ps)`.
+The runner's strict output parser rejected that unrecognized notification,
+so the overall receipt is FAIL, zero profiles qualified, and 20 later child
+entries remain NOT_RUN. The receipt's separate `not_run` list names six
+prohibited check categories; it is not the 20 unexecuted matrix children.
+
+Before edits, all 24 original sources, plan, seal and failed receipt plus the
+p0 simulator artifact were archived as 27 SHA-bound files under
+`failure_archive/attempt_01`, with its own archive manifest. The original
+failure, labels, raw stdout, commands and NOT_RUN entries remain unchanged.
+Root independently closed that archive before authorizing a limited repair.
+
+The repair accepts only the fixed path/line317 `$finish called at` notification
+with a decimal time and `(1ps)`, once, after PASS and as the final output line.
+Every other unknown line is still rejected. No RTL, TB, generator, plan,
+fixture, child argv or20-second limit changes. Explicit guards verify the
+entire original archive, original failed receipt and four-PASS/twenty-NOT_RUN
+shape, unchanged original 22 other sources, exact 24 commands and ten rejects.
+The repair diff and hashes are in `repair_01`; a new seal also binds the old
+archive. A further failure receives a separate attempt02 archive and cannot
+automatically retry. Root must approve the concrete repair seal before the
+same full 24-child matrix can run. No repair execution is implied by this prose.
